hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"94","Subhaana Allahi wa bihamdihi, 'adada khalqihi, wa ridha nafsihi, wa zinata 'arshihi, wa midaada kalimaatihi. (Thalaatha marraatin idha asbaha). Glory be to Allah and praise Him, as many times as the number of His creation, as much as pleases Himself, as much as the weight of His Throne, and as much as the ink of His words. (Three times in the morning)"
"95","Allāhumma innī as'aluka `ilman nāfi`a, wa rizqan ṭayyiba, wa `amalan mutaqabbala. O Allah, I ask You for knowledge that is of benefit, a good provision, and deeds that will be accepted. (Recite in Arabic upon rising in the morning.) Reference: Ibn As-Sunni, no. 54, Ibn Majah no. 925. Its chain of transmission is good (Hasan), Ibn Al-Qayyim 2/375."
